@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Complex profile diagram — a full MDG-style technology profile with six stereotypes, tagged values, a stereotype generalization tree, and an enumeration of tagged-value datatypes.
'   usecase:      Teach a full Model-Driven-Generation technology profile: stereotype hierarchy, tagged-value datatypes, and enumeration constraints.
'   complexity:   complex
'   domain:       Cloud / MDG
' ============================================================================
title Example Profile Diagram - Complex MDG Profile

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' "CloudProfile" is a technology profile for model-driven code generation.
' Six stereotypes form a generalization tree rooted at «CloudResource».
' Tagged values use typed datatypes, including an ENUMERATION (ScalingPolicy)
' that constrains legal values.  This mirrors what an MDG tool (Sparx EA,
' MagicDraw, Papyrus) ships as a reusable technology profile.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

package "CloudProfile" <<profile>> {

  ' ===== Enumeration used as a tagged-value datatype ==================
  class ScalingPolicy << (E,#C9E7F2) enumeration >> {
    MANUAL
    AUTO_SCALE
    SCHEDULED
  }

  ' ===== Metaclasses extended by the profile ==========================
  class Component << (M,#B4A7E5) metaclass >> { }
  class Node     << (M,#B4A7E5) metaclass >> { }
  class Artifact << (M,#B4A7E5) metaclass >> { }
  class Class    << (M,#B4A7E5) metaclass >> { }

  ' ===== Stereotypes (generalization tree) ============================
  class CloudResource << (S,#F2C9C9) stereotype >> {
    + region : String
    + tags   : String [*]
  }

  class Compute << (S,#F2C9C9) stereotype >> {
    + cpu    : Integer
    + memory : Integer
    + scaling : ScalingPolicy
  }

  class Storage << (S,#F2C9C9) stereotype >> {
    + sizeGB  : Integer
    + encrypted : Boolean
  }

  class Networkable << (S,#F2C9C9) stereotype >> {
    + cidr : String
    + ports : Integer [*]
  }

  class Container << (S,#F2C9C9) stereotype >> {
    + image : String
  }

  class Function << (S,#F2C9C9) stereotype >> {
    + runtime : String
    + handler : String
    + timeout : Integer
  }

  ' ===== Stereotype generalization (inherit tagged values) ============
  Compute   --|> CloudResource
  Storage   --|> CloudResource
  Networkable --|> CloudResource
  Container --|> Compute
  Function  --|> Compute

  ' ===== Extensions (stereotype -> metaclass) =========================
  CloudResource ..> Component : <<extend>>
  Networkable   ..> Node      : <<extend>>
  Container     ..> Artifact  : <<extend>>
  Function      ..> Class     : <<extend>>

  ' ===== Tagged-value datatype binding =================================
  ' Compute.scaling is typed by the ScalingPolicy enumeration.
  Compute ..> ScalingPolicy : taggedValue type
}

note right of CloudResource
  <b>Stereotype generalization tree</b>
  CloudResource is the root; Compute,
  Storage, Networkable inherit region
  and tags.  Container & Function
  SPECIALISE Compute, inheriting cpu,
  memory, scaling too.  Apply the
  MOST specific stereotype to an
  element to get every applicable tag.
end note

note bottom of ScalingPolicy
  <b>Enumeration datatype</b>
  ScalingPolicy is an Enumeration used
  as the TYPE of the Compute.scaling
  tagged value.  Legal values are
  constrained to MANUAL, AUTO_SCALE,
  SCHEDULED — the profile enforces
  this at application time.
end note

@enduml
